Original failure capture; public calls in each scenario share one fresh process.

Scenario: rejected shortage must preserve stock
call: run_stock(["reserve bolt 3"])
got: {"result": "reserved=3; bolt=5"}
want: {"result": "reserved=3; bolt=5"}
call: run_stock(["reserve bolt 6"])
got: {"raises": "ValueError"}
want: {"raises": "ValueError"}
call: run_stock(["show bolt"])
got: {"result": "bolt=-1"}
want: {"result": "bolt=5"}
call: run_stock(["show nut"])
got: {"result": "nut=5"}
want: {"result": "nut=5"}

Scenario: negative reservation must preserve stock
call: run_stock(["reserve nut 2"])
got: {"result": "reserved=2; nut=3"}
want: {"result": "reserved=2; nut=3"}
call: run_stock(["reserve nut -2"])
got: {"raises": "ValueError"}
want: {"raises": "ValueError"}
call: run_stock(["show nut"])
got: {"result": "nut=5"}
want: {"result": "nut=3"}
call: run_stock(["show bolt"])
got: {"result": "bolt=8"}
want: {"result": "bolt=8"}
